omashiri-remote-unlock
======================

Unlock a LUKS root over SSH at boot.

1. Put the public keys allowed to unlock in /etc/dropbear/root_key
   (authorized_keys format, one per line, mode 0600).
2. Set the initramfs network in the kernel command line, e.g.
   ip=dhcp   or   ip=192.168.1.10::192.168.1.1:255.255.255.0::eth0:none
3. Rebuild the initramfs: mkinitcpio -P
4. At boot: ssh root@<host>, then the passphrase prompt appears.

The hooks come from /etc/mkinitcpio.conf.d/50-omashiri-remote-unlock.conf.
